WEBVTT

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:52.160
I can't figure it out the cause for the unusual temperature increase at the South Pole at all.

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:01.430
Are you that worried, Karen?

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:03.040
Subaru.

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:05.580
This is the legendary giant glacier, isn't it?

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:06.420
Yeah.

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:12.150
It's said that this glacier won't melt until the end of the world.

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:14.250
It's like a guardian spirit for the South Pole.

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:18.430
We have to protect this legendary glacier at all costs.

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:26.380
The reason why I'm here is to investigate temperature anomalies and to protect the South Pole.

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:29.320
But now...

00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:31.270
Now...?

00:02:31.270 --> 00:02:34.370
Now, I have more to protect.

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:36.580
Subaru...

00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:51.140
I would never have guessed that the giant glacier would start to melt.

00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:56.500
The Prayer of the Seven Seas

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:08.070
How is it? Only I, Hanon-san, could wear anything and make it suit me!

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:12.140
I-I guess it's about right.

00:03:12.350 --> 00:03:14.910
Lucia, that's really cute!

00:03:14.910 --> 00:03:15.880
You think so?

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:17.810
Rina!

00:03:18.830 --> 00:03:22.280
No matter what, this skirt is too short.

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:25.480
It's great! The length of the skirt is just right!

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:26.720
It's perfect! It's perfect!

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:29.130
It really suits you, Rina!

00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:32.200
That's right! When guys see those legs, they'll melt!

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:34.310
I-Is that so?

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:36.610
Eh? Rina is smiling!

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:39.570
Who are you thinking about?

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:42.800
I knew it! I'm not buying it!

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:44.990
There's no way I'm buying this outfit!

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:47.470
Huh?

00:03:48.730 --> 00:03:49.840
Hippo!

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:52.810
Wait a minute, Hippo!

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:56.100
Why aren't you wearing any clothes?

00:03:58.890 --> 00:04:00.110
"Penpen?"

00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:02.370
I don't think that's Hippo.

00:04:06.590 --> 00:04:10.660
Karen sent you all the way here from the South Pole?

00:04:11.530 --> 00:04:13.220
You're Pipi-san, aren't you?

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:16.620
It must have been hard for a girl like you to come from that far away.

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:21.280
Pipi-chan said there's something wrong at the South Pole.

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:25.910
She said that it's become unusually warm and the glaciers there are slowly melting.

00:04:26.290 --> 00:04:32.200
Even worse, she said that the legendary giant glacier {that couldn't melt }is beginning to show signs of melting.

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:36.540
Eh!? You mean the legendary giant glacier at the South Pole that's said to be a guardian spirit?

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:45.430
If that giant glacier really is starting to melt, it wouldn't be unexpected if we find the whole world under water.

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:48.810
In any case, we need to hurry and get to the South Pole.

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:52.340
Karen's in trouble. We can't just ignore this.

00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:07.590
She said we're almost at the South Pole!

00:05:07.590 --> 00:05:09.780
It's not as cold as I thought it would be.

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:13.240
Considering that this is the Antarctic Ocean, the water temperature really is unusual.

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:15.060
Everyone! Over here!

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:19.020
Lucia! Hanon! Rina!

00:05:19.020 --> 00:05:20.150
Karen!

00:05:20.150 --> 00:05:23.510
Everyone! You've all come! Thank you!

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:28.440
I'm sorry, everyone.

00:05:28.880 --> 00:05:31.490
To tell you the truth, I should let you rest a bit.

00:05:31.490 --> 00:05:33.830
If we rest, we'll be wasting time.

00:05:33.830 --> 00:05:36.550
That's right! You don't have to worry about us, Karen.

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:41.740
Here it is. This is the legendary giant glacier of the South Pole.

00:05:42.700 --> 00:05:45.280
Wow! It's huge!

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:48.190
This isn't a glacier, it's an ice mountain.

00:05:48.190 --> 00:05:51.480
But now this giant glacier is starting to melt.

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:54.160
Right now, the South Pole is experiencing an unusual rise in temperature.

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:56.270
There must be a reason for this.

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:06.000
What's going on!? Is it an earthquake?

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:07.130
No, it isn't.

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:08.480
Then what happened just now?

00:06:08.690 --> 00:06:12.180
That must have been a part of the giant glacier that broke off and fell.

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:14.250
Hey!

00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:16.650
A voice came from over there!

00:06:20.050 --> 00:06:22.300
Subaru! What's going on?

00:06:22.300 --> 00:06:23.660
Ah, Karen.

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:27.680
A crack opened up when the tremors started, and my foot got stuck in it.

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:31.070
Are you okay? Here, let me help you.

00:06:31.070 --> 00:06:32.880
Wow, he's perfect!

00:06:33.190 --> 00:06:36.010
When did Karen find such a wonderful guy?

00:06:38.920 --> 00:06:41.330
Thank you, Karen. You saved me.

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:44.460
My goodness! Subaru, you're so clumsy.

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:48.000
Hey, Karen! Introduce him to us! Who is he?

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:51.500
Oh, I'm sorry. I haven't introduced myself.

00:06:51.940 --> 00:06:55.370
I'm here on behalf of a British research group. I'm Subaru Carraford Hashimoto.

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:57.560
A British research group?

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:00.870
I'm here to investigate the unusual temperature increase here in the South Pole.

00:07:00.870 --> 00:07:03.660
Wow! He's an elite.

00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:05.230
He's so cool!

00:07:05.230 --> 00:07:06.780
Nice to meet you...

00:07:08.140 --> 00:07:09.180
Ahh!

00:07:09.180 --> 00:07:10.850
My foot's stuck again!

00:07:10.850 --> 00:07:13.080
Subaru, what {in the world }are you doing!?

00:07:13.290 --> 00:07:15.590
It seems he's very good at being clumsy.

00:07:17.110 --> 00:07:19.470
I don't know what to do with you.

00:07:19.470 --> 00:07:22.150
Ugh. Sorry about that.

00:07:22.340 --> 00:07:25.410
He isn't as cool as I thought he was, but he seems to be a good person.

00:07:25.410 --> 00:07:29.110
Yeah. He and Karen seem to get along quite well.

00:07:29.610 --> 00:07:32.990
By the way, this is the first time I've seen you guys.

00:07:32.990 --> 00:07:34.980
Are you also here as part of a research group, like Karen?

00:07:34.980 --> 00:07:36.790
Part of a research group?

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:39.310
Karen must have told him that.

00:07:39.310 --> 00:07:40.440
Oh, I see.

00:07:40.750 --> 00:07:42.760
So, where are you from?

00:07:43.090 --> 00:07:44.740
Uhh...

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:46.430
Over there!

00:07:51.130 --> 00:07:52.670
W-We messed up...

00:07:53.390 --> 00:07:54.300
Over that way!

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:57.900
We're here to research something else.

00:07:58.860 --> 00:08:00.880
S-Sorry, Subaru...

00:08:01.720 --> 00:08:04.710
I-In any case, I'd better go!

00:08:05.010 --> 00:08:05.460
Karen!

00:08:05.460 --> 00:08:06.300
Eh?

00:08:07.080 --> 00:08:08.730
So... see you later.

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:10.320
Y-Yeah.

00:08:14.950 --> 00:08:16.850
Hey, you two.

00:08:16.850 --> 00:08:21.360
If Subaru gets suspicious about what we're doing, what do you plan to do?

00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:24.980
Now, now. Karen, please forgive them for what just happened.

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:28.420
So, Karen, do you like Subaru-san?

00:08:28.420 --> 00:08:31.360
What... are you saying all of a sudden?

00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:34.340
N-Now is not the time to be talking about that!

00:08:35.020 --> 00:08:38.020
I-I'm the Mermaid Princess of the Antarctic Ocean!

00:08:38.020 --> 00:08:40.480
It's my duty to protect the South Pole!

00:08:40.480 --> 00:08:44.090
So, Karen, how do you feel about Subaru-san?

00:08:44.510 --> 00:08:45.670
How do I feel...

00:08:46.860 --> 00:08:49.010
Subaru is truly a good person.

00:08:49.010 --> 00:08:55.340
He's warmer and kinder than any other person that I've met.

00:08:55.340 --> 00:08:59.510
He cares, more than anyone else, about the South Pole.

00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:02.550
So that means that you like him, don't you?

00:09:03.890 --> 00:09:06.920
Well, you could say that, I guess.

00:09:16.710 --> 00:09:17.600
Lucia!

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:19.170
Lucia!

00:09:19.170 --> 00:09:20.240
Lucia!

00:09:20.720 --> 00:09:21.950
Lucia!

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:23.770
Lucia-san!

00:09:25.240 --> 00:09:28.680
Rina, what should we do? Lucia has... Lucia has...

00:09:28.680 --> 00:09:30.080
Hanon, calm down.

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:34.140
Karen, let's start searching for places that this crack could lead to.

00:09:34.140 --> 00:09:35.090
Alright.

00:09:45.010 --> 00:09:48.290
I-It seems I got lucky. Thank goodness.

00:09:48.960 --> 00:09:50.530
But, where am I?

00:09:51.160 --> 00:09:54.710
It looks like a cave was created from the melting glacier.

00:09:55.040 --> 00:09:56.800
The water temperature is unusually high.

00:09:57.760 --> 00:10:01.480
Huh? There seems to be a noise from a machine coming from the water.

00:10:03.690 --> 00:10:04.660
What's that?

00:10:04.660 --> 00:10:07.350
That machine is pumping out a large amount of hot water!

00:10:08.260 --> 00:10:13.910
So, is that large machine the reason why the South Pole is warmer than usual?

00:10:13.910 --> 00:10:15.390
Oh my, what a surprise.

00:10:16.180 --> 00:10:19.890
Who would have thought that we'd run into the Pink Pearl Mermaid Princess here?

00:10:19.890 --> 00:10:21.500
How true.

00:10:21.500 --> 00:10:23.080
Sheshe and Mimi!

00:10:23.080 --> 00:10:25.300
I knew that you two were behind this!

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:27.680
Mimi, capture her.

00:10:28.030 --> 00:10:30.510
Okay! Reverse!

00:10:37.250 --> 00:10:41.530
We can give Mikeru-sama a nice present, Sister Sheshe.

00:10:41.530 --> 00:10:42.520
Yeah!

00:10:42.520 --> 00:10:46.920
Maybe the other Mermaid Princesses are nearby.

00:10:47.970 --> 00:10:49.590
Lucia!

00:10:49.590 --> 00:10:50.730
Lucia!

00:10:51.240 --> 00:10:52.610
Did you find her over there?

00:10:52.610 --> 00:10:53.660
I couldn't find her.

00:10:53.870 --> 00:10:55.520
She's not here either.

00:10:56.570 --> 00:10:59.740
It's all my fault because I asked Lucia to come to the South Pole.

00:10:59.740 --> 00:11:04.680
If... if something happens to Lucia... I...

00:11:06.540 --> 00:11:08.890
Karen, Lucia is definitely all right!

00:11:08.890 --> 00:11:10.950
What would we do if we didn't believe that?

00:11:10.950 --> 00:11:14.740
We Mermaid Princesses are seven beings united in our hearts, correct?

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:19.220
If something happened to Lucia, there is no way that we would not know about it.

00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:21.120
Rina... Hanon...

00:11:22.650 --> 00:11:25.470
Pipi! Send a message to everyone in the ocean.

00:11:25.780 --> 00:11:27.360
We're going to need everyone's help.

00:11:32.150 --> 00:11:33.970
The tremors have finally stopped.

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:37.960
I wonder if Karen is okay after all those tremors.

00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:43.250
But at the rate this is going, the legendary glacier is really going to melt away.

00:11:43.250 --> 00:11:46.150
Eh? What's this about a legendary glacier?

00:11:46.150 --> 00:11:48.790
Please tell us about it.

00:11:48.790 --> 00:11:50.590
W-Who are you?

00:11:58.510 --> 00:12:00.960
Presented by Licca and Wasurenai-Fansubs

00:12:14.220 --> 00:12:16.910
Lucia! Lucia! Wake up!

00:12:17.400 --> 00:12:18.150
Seira.

00:12:18.480 --> 00:12:21.650
At the rate this is going, the legendary giant glacier will be melt completely.

00:12:22.240 --> 00:12:24.120
We need your power.

00:12:25.010 --> 00:12:27.680
Wait, Seira! Seira!

00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:31.130
This is...

00:12:47.790 --> 00:12:50.170
Where... is this?

00:12:54.400 --> 00:12:57.680
Welcome to my realm.

00:12:58.140 --> 00:13:02.760
I never would have thought I'd see a Mermaid Princess here.

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:07.330
Mikeru! Are you responsible for melting the glacier at the South Pole?

00:13:07.330 --> 00:13:09.210
Why are you doing such a thing?

00:13:09.560 --> 00:13:15.120
In order to purify this world and to take it back from humans.

00:13:15.470 --> 00:13:17.780
In order to return it to a world of justice.

00:13:18.420 --> 00:13:19.970
I won't let you do that!

00:13:19.970 --> 00:13:22.210
We'll find a way to stop you!

00:13:23.430 --> 00:13:25.170
Only if they make it in time.

00:13:25.990 --> 00:13:27.300
Who are you?

00:13:27.300 --> 00:13:29.820
Instead of asking who I am, why don't you look down there?{your feet?}

00:13:30.920 --> 00:13:32.010
That's...

00:13:33.310 --> 00:13:34.420
Subaru-san!

00:13:35.030 --> 00:13:37.210
What are you doing to him!?

00:13:37.210 --> 00:13:41.850
Don't worry. We've just put his heart to sleep.

00:13:41.850 --> 00:13:45.100
Now he's one of our good allies.

00:13:46.600 --> 00:13:54.370
Not only did he tell us the legend of the giant glacier, but he also has increased the power of our machine.

00:13:54.370 --> 00:13:55.760
How true.

00:13:55.760 --> 00:13:56.670
That's awful.

00:13:56.670 --> 00:14:02.490
Now, Mermaid Princess. Hand over your heart for me to keep.

00:14:02.490 --> 00:14:06.560
This is in order to create a beautiful new world.

00:14:06.560 --> 00:14:07.460
No!

00:14:07.810 --> 00:14:11.030
I'm never going to give my heart to you!

00:14:11.030 --> 00:14:13.090
I'll show you that I can use my own way!

00:14:13.090 --> 00:14:16.900
I will protect the peace of the ocean and the world where the people most precious to me live!

00:14:17.380 --> 00:14:23.340
There's no point arguing. Stay there and watch as the new world is born.

00:14:23.500 --> 00:14:27.280
Here we go! Target the legendary giant glacier!

00:14:27.490 --> 00:14:29.160
Turbo switch, on!

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:38.460
If you put out that much hot water, all of the glaciers at the South Pole will melt!

00:14:38.930 --> 00:14:40.890
Stop! Stop!

00:14:45.980 --> 00:14:48.110
The glaciers have suddenly started to crack.

00:14:48.480 --> 00:14:49.950
It'll be bad if this continues!

00:14:52.360 --> 00:14:54.140
Aqua Pearl Voice!

00:14:56.790 --> 00:14:58.450
Green Pearl Voice!

00:15:00.680 --> 00:15:02.480
Purple Pearl Voice!

00:15:05.760 --> 00:15:08.520
Subaru! What are you doing in a place like this?

00:15:09.770 --> 00:15:11.190
Sheshe! Mimi!

00:15:11.190 --> 00:15:13.180
I knew it was you two!

00:15:13.180 --> 00:15:14.390
What did you do to Subaru?

00:15:15.840 --> 00:15:17.290
Ask him yourself.

00:15:19.730 --> 00:15:22.240
Stop, Subaru!

00:15:22.240 --> 00:15:25.610
Nothing that you say to him will do you any good.

00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:29.730
He's been hypnotized and will only listen to us.

00:15:29.920 --> 00:15:31.140
Subaru...

00:15:35.100 --> 00:15:38.280
Karen, take him to a safe place.

00:15:41.750 --> 00:15:45.800
The melting will only stop if you defeat us.

00:15:45.800 --> 00:15:48.460
But you're running short on time.

00:15:52.290 --> 00:15:53.830
What should I do!?

00:15:56.210 --> 00:15:58.390
You can't give up that easily, Lucia.

00:15:59.390 --> 00:16:00.870
Sing, Lucia.

00:16:01.460 --> 00:16:03.030
Don't give up! Sing!

00:16:03.030 --> 00:16:03.940
Sara!

00:16:04.410 --> 00:16:07.040
Sing, Lucia! Please!

00:16:10.910 --> 00:16:15.920
That's right! Before I give up and do nothing, I can still sing!

00:16:27.270 --> 00:16:28.960
Pink Pearl Voice!

00:16:35.400 --> 00:16:37.860
Pichi Pichi Voice Live Start!

00:16:53.000 --> 00:16:54.030
That's useless.

00:17:36.600 --> 00:17:39.370
Lucia, we got the message from Karen.

00:17:39.370 --> 00:17:41.450
We'll sing with you.

00:17:41.450 --> 00:17:43.440
Please, Lucia. Don't give up!

00:17:49.710 --> 00:17:51.720
Indigo Pearl Voice!

00:17:53.130 --> 00:17:55.110
Yellow Pearl Voice!

00:18:10.480 --> 00:18:12.600
What is this? What are these other songs?

00:18:12.850 --> 00:18:15.700
Is this the singing from the other Mermaid Princesses?

00:18:15.700 --> 00:18:17.840
Where is this singing coming from?

00:18:18.020 --> 00:18:19.410
This singing is...

00:18:19.410 --> 00:18:22.250
It's Lucia! And we've also got Noelle and Coco!

00:18:22.250 --> 00:18:24.560
Hanon, let's sing!

00:18:24.560 --> 00:18:25.320
Yeah!

00:18:45.520 --> 00:18:46.480
Everyone.

00:19:14.370 --> 00:19:16.500
Huh? Why?

00:19:16.500 --> 00:19:18.340
What's going on?

00:19:22.550 --> 00:19:25.190
What the? My dimension is about to fall apart.

00:19:25.740 --> 00:19:30.110
Is this the full power of the Mermaid Princesses?

00:19:30.640 --> 00:19:35.410
Please, use your power to prevent the destruction of the world.

00:19:35.410 --> 00:19:37.250
Everyone, hang in there!

00:20:50.760 --> 00:20:52.350
Thank you, Lucia.

00:20:52.760 --> 00:20:56.680
This is the heart of a pure, loving nature.{This is the heart of loving the state of unadulterated nature.}

00:20:57.410 --> 00:20:58.860
It's really wonderful.

00:21:01.080 --> 00:21:01.880
Seira.

00:21:02.840 --> 00:21:04.070
Lucia!

00:21:05.700 --> 00:21:06.870
Lucia!

00:21:06.870 --> 00:21:09.370
I'm glad that you're okay!

00:21:09.370 --> 00:21:10.490
Lucia!

00:21:16.060 --> 00:21:18.750
It seems that the warming trend at the South Pole has halted.

00:21:19.090 --> 00:21:22.860
I'll return to my country and present my data to the research group.

00:21:23.640 --> 00:21:25.940
We'll meet again, Karen.

00:21:27.400 --> 00:21:30.340
Yeah. We definitely will.

00:21:47.450 --> 00:21:48.390
Karen.

00:21:48.390 --> 00:21:50.440
Is it fine to just let him go like that?

00:21:51.030 --> 00:21:54.720
I think Subaru-san loves you, Karen.

00:21:55.340 --> 00:21:59.630
It's fine. Subaru and I would be a human and mermaid couple.

00:22:00.210 --> 00:22:04.740
If I were with Subaru, things like this would happen to him all the time.

00:22:06.740 --> 00:22:08.880
Therefore, it's fine this way.

00:22:08.880 --> 00:22:09.950
Karen...

00:23:51.050 --> 00:23:53.780
Stand up, Karen! Are you only capable of that?

00:23:53.780 --> 00:23:57.110
Onee-san! I'm a clumsy turtle!

00:23:57.110 --> 00:23:58.820
You're not a turtle! You're a mermaid, aren't you?

00:23:58.820 --> 00:24:01.530
A serve from the Arctic Ocean!

00:24:01.530 --> 00:24:02.720
I'm beaten.

00:24:02.720 --> 00:24:03.990
Tears have been shed...

00:24:04.180 --> 00:24:05.750
I feel horrible...

00:24:05.750 --> 00:24:06.770
Onee-san!

00:24:06.770 --> 00:24:08.900
We'll shout at the evening sun!

00:24:09.290 --> 00:24:11.960
Pichi Pichi Voice Live Start!

00:24:12.320 --> 00:24:15.640
Next time on Mermaid Melody Pichi Pichi Pitch Pure:

00:24:15.640 --> 00:24:17.990
It's Summertime! Everyone Get Together!

00:24:17.990 --> 00:24:19.790
Is this the wrong program?
